   "output": "{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"eta (H6, OPS-A4-37, OPS-A4-55): eta-rules version 0.6.7. You are in an eta repo. Your entry skill follows. Load the skill it names for each moment, and fetch the pages that skill names before you act.\\n\\n# Using the eta rules\\n\\nThis plugin holds no rules (OPS-A4-17). Each skill names one group of rules on the eta Docs pages. Fetch those pages by ID and read them before you act. A hook refuses a guarded action until you have fetched them in this session (H13). Where hooks don't run, as in the Claude app, nothing checks this, so read them anyway.\\n\\n## 1. Wakes when\\n- A session starts in an eta repo (H6).\\n- The eta-rules session-start line is missing or names an old version (the restart check).\\n- Your runtime runs no hooks: the Claude app, and Codex and Cursor until they are tested.\\n- A request names a work key (ETA-123).\\n- You are about to write in Notion, Linear, GitHub, Slack or Figma.\\n\\n## 2. Read first\\nOpen each page by its ID. Never find it by searching its title: snapshot copies of these pages exist.\\n- Agents (A4) (https://app.notion.com/p/3f28f1ec11b481f3ac03c33704d8a63e): A4.2 and A4.5; OPS-A4-35, 37, 51 and 55.\\n- Entry and the lightmap (F0) (https://app.notion.com/p/3f28f1ec11b48191af1ef6be90623598): OPS-F0-22 and 31.\\n- Code and doc (https://app.notion.com/p/3f28f1ec11b48134b2effda38de1fd5b): OPS-F2-53 and 59.\\n- Work (A2) (https://app.notion.com/p/3f28f1ec11b48123aabfe1e4635d371f): the base skills below name the parts to read.\\n- Docs (A1) (https://app.notion.com/p/3f28f1ec11b4819ead93ef135e75362f): the same.\\n- Communications (A3) (https://app.notion.com/p/3f28f1ec11b481f186ebfa6ff95e4a5d): the same.\\n- How we work (the overview): https://app.notion.com/p/3f28f1ec11b48136b7dec061ebba2df2\\n\\n## 3. Then\\n1. Run the restart check before anything else (OPS-A4-35, 55).\\n2. Where your runtime runs no hooks, read the pages yourself (OPS-A4-51). Build no code there (OPS-F2-59).\\n3. Check the stamp: a work issue key in context (OPS-F0-22, 31). With no key, load eta-ask.\\n4. A page is wrong, silent, or disagrees with another: post the BLOCKED line and stop (OPS-F2-53).\\n5. Send the moment to its skill.\\n\\n| You are about to | Load |\\n|---|---|\\n| write with no work key in context, or answer where a piece goes | eta-ask |\\n| start or continue work that has a key | eta-lightmap |\\n| do a step and post its output | eta-do-a-step |\\n| do something the lightmap doesn't hav",
